 "content": "# Continual-ARC task 7ffba523\n\nObserved rule from the demo and confirmed test: identify each hollow, axis-aligned rectangular outline; preserve the outline and background, and fill its interior uniformly based on the interior area's parity: odd number of rows/columns (the observed cases were 1x1 and 5x5) -> color 7; even (2x2, 4x4) -> color 2. Frame color does not determine fill in the example. In the test, the 6-frame's 4x4 interior was filled with 2, and the 4-frame's 5x5 interior with 7. Demo showed this applied independently to multiple rectangles while leaving unrelated cells unchanged.\n"
